{"schema_version":1,"search_id":"e3e0e3d1c47b4e15b457b9c843436deb","seq":21,"turn":0,"at_ms":7168.267417000607,"type":"search_finished","result":{"question":{"content":[{"kind":"text","text":"Did last month's latency spike come from the new reranker, and is it fixed?"}]},"hits":[{"hit":{"doc_id":"INC-4821","source":"incidents","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"search-api p95 elevated across all regions\n\nOpened by on-call (Priya Raman) at 09:12 UTC after the SLO burn alert fired. search-api p95 latency climbed from ~180 ms to ~640 ms starting early Sept 14 and is holding there. p50 is only slightly up. Error rate is flat, so requests succeed but slowly. CPU on the search-api pods is up ~35%. Checked the CDN and the edge cache: both look normal. No config pushes in the last 12 hours. Mitigation so far: scaled search-api from 24 to 36 pods, which took p95 down to ~520 ms but did not clear it. Root cause: not yet identified. Leaving open for the search team to investigate on Monday. Customer impact: slower search results pages, some timeouts on the mobile app's type-ahead."}],"metadata":{"opened":"2026-09-14","service":"search-api","severity":"SEV2","status":"resolved","title":"search-api p95 elevated across all regions"},"raw_score":0.6489217206265213,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c0","rank":4},{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c3","rank":0}]},"score":0.907711,"p_relevant":0.9,"rationale":"Describes search-api latency spike in mid-September.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"DASH-W38-search","source":"dashboards","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"search-api weekly SLO report, week 38\n\nWeek of Sept 14–20. p95 was 610 ms Monday to Thursday morning, above the 300 ms SLO; from Sept 18 afternoon p95 dropped to 176 ms and stayed at baseline through Sunday. p50 98 ms for the week. Availability 99.95%. Error budget: 38% used this week."}],"metadata":{"service":"search-api","week":"2026-W38","week_start":"2026-09-14","week_end":"2026-09-20","title":"search-api weekly SLO report, week 38"},"raw_score":0.015045248868778281,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c5","rank":6}]},"score":0.855892,"p_relevant":0.9,"rationale":"Search-api weekly report for week 38 shows latency spike dropping on Sept 18.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"DEP-0908-01","source":"deploys","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"GPU node pool for reranker v2\n\nInfra: dedicated GPU node pool for reranker v2 inference, 6 nodes."}],"metadata":{"date":"2026-09-08","service":"search-api","version":"4.11.1","pr":null,"author":"Ravi Shah","title":"GPU node pool for reranker v2"},"raw_score":2.245522178994585,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c4","rank":5}]},"score":0.766588,"p_relevant":0.8,"rationale":"GPU node pool deployment for reranker v2.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"PR-1187","source":"pull_requests","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"Roll out reranker v2 to all search traffic\n\nThis turns on reranker v2 (the cross-encoder model) for 100% of search requests, up from the 5% experiment. Offline NDCG@10 is +4.1% over v1. Batch size is set to 64 to keep GPU utilisation high. Rollout is behind the reranker_v2 flag so we can turn it off. Reviewers: @lortiz @pramam."}],"metadata":{"number":1187,"merged":"2026-09-12","service":"search-api","author":"Marcus Chen","title":"Roll out reranker v2 to all search traffic"},"raw_score":0.6295955411460765,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c1","rank":7}]},"score":0.765218,"p_relevant":0.8,"rationale":"Rolls out reranker v2 to 100% of traffic, relevant to search latency.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"DEP-0805-02","source":"deploys","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"search-api reranker v2 shadow mode\n\nStarts reranker v2 in shadow mode: reranker v2 scores are logged, reranker v1 still ranks results."}],"metadata":{"date":"2026-08-05","service":"search-api","version":"4.10.2","pr":1178,"author":"Marcus Chen","title":"search-api reranker v2 shadow mode"},"raw_score":2.7298446891658714,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c4"